  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Check your avocado is ripe before starting this recipe (see Kitchen hack). Thinly slice the onion. Peel the sweet potato and cut into 2cm chunks. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Drain and rinse half the beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842472/photos/large/163920_1-f9548f878abed95a0e1bc0a36e0e8539.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start sauce: Heat 1 tbs olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion and sweet potato, stirring, for 3-4 mins until the onion is softened. Add the garlic, Tex-Mex seasoning and half the tomato paste and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842473/photos/large/163920_2-75f68b48cf73e59d1015fef886568333.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer sauce: Add the tomatoes, beans and 125ml (½ cup) water to the sweet potato mixture and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium-low, cover and cook, stirring occasionally, for 17 mins. Cook, uncovered, for a further 5 mins or until slightly thickened and the sweet potato is tender. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842474/photos/large/163920_3-ccf8dab510b712d6f333f2caf921715d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook eggs: Make 2 egg-sized indents in the tomato mixture and crack 2 eggs into the indents. Cook, covered, for 3-4 mins until the eggs are cooked to your liking. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842475/photos/large/163920_4-0376790b6c2716e22d758b6ae88d2b39.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Slice the avocado. Divide the shakshuka among bowls and serve with the avocado and corn chips. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842476/photos/large/163920_5-cb6b88601ff7e1599622ce074d52ca22.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen hack: To speed up the ripening process, put the avocado in a paper bag and loosely close, then leave on the kitchen bench for a day or two. Add a banana to the bag to make the avocado ripen faster.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3842477/photos/large/163920_6-0d0777423a56064c868a37958cd89901.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
